! ======================================================================
! test_v1101_h2o_b3lyp_rt_kick -- RT-TDDFT ladder step 3 for a GLOBAL
! HYBRID: complex exchange (c_HF = 0.2) and the XC quadrature drive the
! same trajectory; the kick spectrum must reproduce the Casida B3LYP
! states.  Kick along y (b2 states) -- the strongest transition of the
! spectrum plus a weaker neighbor that probes the Lorentzian-overlap
! systematics.
!
! H2O/B3LYP/STO-3G, %grid 1 (SAME grid in the Casida kernel and the RT
! propagation -- consistent two-road comparison), kick kappa = 1e-3,
! 5000 steps of dt = 0.2 (T = 1000 au), gamma = 0.006 (gamma*T = 6),
! %rt_pc_maxiter 4 (dt = 0.2 + strong kick wants ~3-4 PC iterations).
!
! Reference (v1.10.1, 1 thread, reference BLAS; ~2 min propagation):
!   SCF total energy (grid 1):   -75.296239718632
!   RT self-check |dE|:           ~3e-14
!   Casida y-polarized states:
!     state 4:  w = 0.657841 Ha,  f = 0.06172
!     state 5:  w = 0.791973 Ha,  f = 0.94430
!   RT peaks (kick along y):
!     w = 0.65805 Ha,  f-contribution = 0.063842   (dw = +2.1e-4,
!         df = +3.4 % -- the tail of the 15x stronger neighbor at
!         gamma/separation ~ 0.045 adds (gamma/D)^2-class height;
!         documented Lorentzian-overlap systematics)
!     w = 0.79195 Ha,  f-contribution = 0.944004   (dw = -2.3e-5 Ha,
!         df = -0.03 % -- the hybrid oracle lands)
!   Post-kick energy conservation: max |E(t)-E(0)| ~ 9.2e-11 Ha over
!   5000 steps with complex K + XC.
! ======================================================================
%method  B3LYP
%basis   sto-3g
%grid    1
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%scf_ptol 1e-9
%tddft   6
%rt_tddft 5000
%rt_dt    0.2
%rt_kick  0.001
%rt_kick_dir y
%rt_gamma 0.006
%rt_pc_maxiter 4
%rt_wmax  1.2
%rt_print_every 2500
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
H    0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
H    0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
